  "releaseNotes": "get_child_device_list responses from hubs/strips with more children than fit in a single page previously only returned the first page's children; the sum/start_index pagination fields the device reports were parsed but never acted on. KasaDevice.UpdateAsync now detects when sum exceeds the number of children already received and issues additional get_child_device_list requests with increasing start_index until every child has been retrieved (stopping early if a page comes back empty), merging all pages into a single, complete child list before child-state enrichment runs. Devices with child lists that fit in one page are unaffected.",
